  "rationale": "Genome-wide in vivo knockout screen (87,690 guides, up to 4 per gene, 800 non-targeting) in encephalitogenic rat CD4+ T-MBP cells transferred into Lewis rats; on day 3 the cells were recovered from blood, spleen, spinal cord leptomeninges and parenchyma of three animals (R1-R3). Columns are self-named by replicate and tissue and match the GSM titles. Knockouts that impair entry into the CNS are depleted in parenchyma (and meninges) relative to blood, the authors' MvsB and PvsB comparisons. Tissues of one animal come from the same transferred cell pool and correlate by animal (Spearman 0.94-0.97 within R2 and R3), so rat enters the model as a paired term (2 residual df). Culture and plasmid libraries are not used.",
